[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124856,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Combined naevus is a benign melanocytic neoplasm with two or more phenotypically distinct tumour cell populations that is not a WNT-activated, <em>BAP1</em>-inactivated, or pigmented epithelioid melanocytoma; a proliferating nodule; or a collision tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124857,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8720/0 Combined naevus</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124858,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F20.Y &amp; XH0DU8 Other specific types of melanocytic naevus &amp; Combined naevus</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124859,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> biphenotypic naevus; clonal naevus; naevus with phenotypic heterogeneity; naevus with dermal epithelioid component.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> inverted type&nbsp;A naevus.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124860,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124861,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Combined naevus can occur on any anatomical skin site.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124862,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with combined naevus commonly present with a papule or nodule in a patch or plaque with different pigmentation. There can be a history of recent change.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124863,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Combined naevi account for &lt;&nbsp;1% of melanocytic naevus biopsies. They can develop at any age but typically arise in young adults (mean age: ~30&nbsp;years). There is no sex predilection {15370111}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124864,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124865,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Combined naevi are probably a heterogeneous group of lesions representing forms of stepwise tumour progression similar to melanocytomas, in which a phenotypically distinct subclone arises as a consequence of an additional pathogenic mutation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124866,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124867,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "<p>Typically, there is a compound or dermal naevus of the superficial congenital type with a subpopulation of morphologically distinct cells, usually situated in the superficial dermis. The clone can have varying morphology, but unpigmented epithelioid or hyperpigmented melanocytes are most common. Cytological atypia and mitotic activity are limited {21881487; 15370111}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>The melanocyte population of the background naevus and the subclone may express different immunophenotypes.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry or molecular studies can assist in ruling out <em>BAP1</em>-inactivated, WNT-activated, and pigmented epithelioid melanocytoma, as well as proliferative nodules in congenital naevi.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124868,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124869,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The small size of the clone often limits the potential to study its molecular features. By definition, alterations defining any specific melanocytomas should be absent.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124870,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> two or more cytologically distinct populations of melanocytes in a benign melanocytic lesion that is not a specifically defined melanocytoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> special immunostains may be used to rule out specific melanocytomas (&beta;-catenin, BAP1, PRKAR1A).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124871,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124872,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Combined naevi are benign. Recurrences are rare.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]